; GaiaLabs Retranslation, chapter 30. Dialogue only.

?INCLUDE 'awB0_intro'
awB0_intro.dialogstring_089807! `[BOR:3][DLG:3,4][SIZ:D,5][PRT:@RetranslationTheme0]Within three days of[N]leaving the village, the[N]party reaches an enormous[N]temple.[PAL:0][END]`

?INCLUDE 'awB6_bones'
awB6_bones.dialogstring_08A027! `[BOR:3][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme0]Could this be what remains[N]of a lost explorer that[N]was enchanted by this lost[N]history?[FIN]Oh? They're clutching[N]something like a notebook…[N][PAL:0] Try to read it[N] Leave it be`
awB6_bones.dialogstring_08A094! `[CLD]`
awB6_bones.dialogstring_08A096! `[CLD][BOR:1][DLG:3,B][SIZ:D,7][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1E]We pushed through the[N]jungle and managed to[N]arrive at an aboriginal[N]village.[PAU:1E] We couldn't speak[N]their language, but we[N]stayed with a generous[N]villager, who invited us.[FIN]When we awoke the next[N]morning, we saw that there[N]was no one left but the[N]troop leader Friesel and[N]myself… It was the village[N]of a cannibal tribe![FIN]The troop leader and I[N]took a sidelong glance at[N]bones that our comrades[N]had been reduced to and[N]escaped. We kept[N]wandering; then we[N]discovered Angkor Wat.[FIN]There were rumours that[N]said that there are gods[N]living here who had[N]obtained eternal life, but[N]all that our eyes could[N]see were the figures of[N]demons…[FIN]So now I'll be departing[N]to be by my comrades'[N]sides too… I'll be leaving[N]this world and I won't[N]exist anymore. Is there[N]anyone mourning me?[END]`

?INCLUDE 'sE6_gaia'
sE6_gaia.dialogstring_08E540! `[BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@CastleV051Gaia]When enemies surround thee[N]on solid ground,[N]Earthquaker can stop them[N]all at once.[FIN]`
sE6_gaia.dialogstring_08EE8B! `While dropping from a[N]ledge, attack to strike[N]the ground.[FIN]Earthquaker stuns grounded[N]enemies nearby.`

?INCLUDE 'awBA_bones'
awBA_bones.dialogstring_08A289! `[BOR:3][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme0]The bones of a lost[N]explorer fascinated by [N]something...?[FIN]Something like a journal[N]is under their arm…[N][PAL:0] Try to read it[N] Leave it be`
awBA_bones.dialogstring_08A2EC! `[CLD][BOR:1][DLG:3,D][SIZ:D,6][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1E][SFX:0]        Angkor Wat[N]    Examination Record[N]         -Friesel[N]Angkor Wat is said to be a[N]temple where immortals[N]dwell.[FIN]I reached the main[N]building. The second[N]floor contains a passage[N]filled with light.[FIN]To reach the highest[N]floor, one must cross[N]it, but the brightness[N]is blinding.[FIN]Another legend says those[N]who sought the immortals[N]wore black-quartz lenses.[N]Near the central hall[N]I saw something black[N]shining on the ground.[FIN]Demons forced me away[N]before I could reach it.[N]Perhaps those were the[N]legendary lenses.[FIN]To come this far and stop[N]here is unbearable.[N]If I fail, I hope my child[N]will someday go farther.[END]`

?INCLUDE 'awBC_blinding_light'
awBC_blinding_light.dialogstring_089A65! `[CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@CastleV051Will]Will: You know, after[N]all this, floating glowing[N]crystals are...[FIN]Actually, this is kind[N]of cool.[END]`

?INCLUDE 'sE6_gaia'
sE6_gaia.dialogstring_08E58B! `[CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@CastleV051Gaia]Angkor Wat is called a[N]wandering temple.[WAI][N]Old tales say it hides[N]among the jungle when[N]those unready to find[N]it draw near.[WAI][N]At its highest floor, thou[N]shalt glimpse why thy road[N]has led through so many[N]forgotten places.[FIN][RET]`

?INCLUDE 'awBA_glasses'
awBA_glasses.dialogstring_089FBB! `[DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2]There's something shiny[N]buried in the ground.[FIN]`
awBA_glasses.dialogstring_089FDC! `[CLR][SFX:0][DLY:9]Will finds the[N]Knight's Emblem![PAU:78][END]`

?INCLUDE 'item_use_system'
item_use_system.dialogstring_039984! `[DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4]These are glasses made of[N]black quartz. It seems[N]that even intense light[N]can be blocked with these…[END]`

?INCLUDE 'awBF_spirit_guide'
awBF_spirit_guide.dialogstring_089B8B! `[CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Ancient voice: Will… For[N]thousands of years I have[N]waited for this moment.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@CastleV051Will]Will: Who are you…?[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Ancient voice: The last[N]witness of the people who[N]built this place.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Long before the comet[N]returned, we had learned[N]what its light truly[N]offered.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]It called this a blessing:[N]eternity without sickness[N]or age.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]But eternity inside its[N]vision of perfection was[N]only another kind of[N]servitude.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Not one among us accepted[N]the comet's promise.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]We knew refusal could mean[N]death, or bodies twisted[N]beyond recognition.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Still, every soul among us[N]chose to remain free.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]The comet changed our[N]flesh. It could not claim[N]our wills.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]I alone was chosen to[N]endure.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]I accepted no blessing.[N]I accepted the burden of[N]remembrance.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]One life was sacrificed[N]so that when the comet[N]returned, someone would[N]remember.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Remember why my people[N]chose death before[N]submission.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]They could not defeat it.[N]But neither could it make[N]them kneel.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Now the hour they waited[N]for has come.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Break the will within the[N]comet, Will.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Let humanity choose its[N]own destiny.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Then, at last, my people[N]will have their vengeance.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Close thine eyes.[N]I will show thee a future[N]they died to leave[N]possible.[END]`
awBF_spirit_guide.dialogstring_089C5B! `[CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]Will: What was that…?[N]That world I just saw…[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Ancient voice: One[N]possible future.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@CastleV051Will]Will: Those buildings…[N]They're enormous.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@CastleV051Will]Lights everywhere. Roads[N]stretch farther than I can[N]see.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]And so many people…[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]They're thriving.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]But… Gaia?[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]I can barely feel her.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@CastleV051Will]She seems so far away.[N]Almost forgotten.[FIN][CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@CastleV051Will]…She looks sad.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Ancient voice: It is[N]always sad when a mother[N]must let her children go.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]But sorrow is not regret.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]A loving mother does not[N]keep her children small[N]so they may never leave[N]her.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]She gives them the chance[N]to choose their own road.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]I believe that is Gaia's[N]wish: that humanity have[N]the chance to choose its[N]own road.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Now return to the village.[N]Use this flower to restore[N]those turned to stone.[FIN][CLD][BOR:4][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme17]Let their lives continue.[END]`
awBF_spirit_guide.dialogstring_089E2E! `[BOR:3][DLG:3,4][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme0]The glare fades.[FIN]Will finds the Gorgon[N]Flower in his hand.[END]`
awBF_spirit_guide.dialogstring_089EE0! `[DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][SFX:0][DLY:9]Will takes the Gorgon[N]Flower![PAU:78][END]`

?INCLUDE 'item_use_system'
item_use_system.dialogstring_039A35! `[DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3]Gazed at the Gorgon's[N]flower… However, nothing[N]happened![END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAC_kara'
nvAC_kara.dialogstring_0884A4! `[BOR:7][DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1]Kara: The children taught[N]me a word.[FIN][CLD][BOR:7][DLG:3,13][SIZ:D,3][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1]It seems that "ramapouˮ[N]means "helloˮ in this[N]region.[END]`

?INCLUDE 'item_use_system'
item_use_system.dialogstring_039A63! `[DLG:3,15][SIZ:D,2]Put one Gorgon's petal[N]into the statue's mouth![END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAE_stone_girl1'
nvAE_stone_girl1.dialogstring_089351! `[CLD][DEF][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4]They do not seem to speak[N]Will's language.[N]Their work continues in[N]silence.[END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAE_kara'
nvAE_kara.dialogstring_0895C9! `[CLD][BOR:7][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1]Kara: I spoke with the[N]villagers using gestures.[WAI][N]The animals are returning[N]to the forest.[WAI][N]That means there will[N]be food again.[WAI][N]No one[N]here should ever have to[N]make a choice like that[N]again.[END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAE_stone_girl2'
nvAE_stone_girl2.dialogstring_08942A! `[DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4]The girl is silent and[N]holds out a Red Jewel. She[N]probably intends it as[N]thanks…[FIN][CLD][DLG:3,17][SIZ:D,1]Will receives a Red Jewel![END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAE_erik'
nvAE_erik.dialogstring_089778! `[CLD][BOR:3][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme3]Erik: Even while this[N]village was starving,[N]slave merchants came and[N]kidnapped children.[WAI][N]How could anyone see[N]people hurting like this[N]and think of making money?[END]`

?INCLUDE 'nvAE_kara'
nvAE_kara.dialogstring_08963C! `[CLD][BOR:7][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1]Kara: The villagers led[N]me to a worn trail going[N]northwest. I saw tracks[N]and wagon ruts.[FIN]That trail must lead to[N]where they're taking[N]the captives.[FIN][CLD][BOR:7][DLG:3,11][SIZ:D,4][PRT:@RetranslationTheme1]Let's follow it. Are you[N]ready to go?[N][PAL:0] Yeah, let's go![N] Wait a bit[PAL:4]`
nvAE_kara.dialogstring_0896F9! `[CLR]Well, when you're ready to[N]go, come back here,[N]alright?[END]`
nvAE_kara.dialogstring_08971E! `[CLR]Alright, heaaading out!![END]`
